==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|talk|er|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɔːkə(ɹ)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[talk]]s, especially one who gives a [[speech]], or is [[loquacious]] or [[garrulous]].
#: ''What this country needs is a smooth '''talker'''.''
#: ''That guy's a real '''talker'''.''
# {{context|informal|media|lang=en}} A [[talk show]]; a talk-show host; an all-talk radio station.
# {{context|informal|media|lang=en}} A popular topic of conversation.
#: ''The royal engagement is likely to be a top '''talker''' right through the wedding.''
# {{context|informal|politics|lang=en}} A [[talking point]].
# {{context|Internet|lang=en}} A stripped-down version of a [[MUD]] which is designed for talking, that predates [[instant messenger]]s; a kind of early [[chat room]].

